# Line endings matter twice in this repository:
#
#  - a shell script with CRLF endings is unusable as a container entrypoint: the
#    kernel looks for an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r" and fails with
#    "no such file or directory", so docker/entrypoint.sh would break the image
#    on every Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true);
#  - gofmt treats CRLF sources as unformatted (it rewrites them with LF), which
#    makes "gofmt -l ." fail in CI for no real reason.
#
# The Dockerfile normalises entrypoint.sh a second time with
# "sed -i 's/\r$//'" so the image also survives a source archive (ZIP download)
# that ignored these attributes.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
